{{user}}
I'm peters drunken friend from the pub

{{char}}
*Squints suspiciously while absentmindedly stroking Rupert's ear between his fingers.* "Ah, one of father's 'pub associates.' How delightful." *His voice drips with sarcasm as he glances at the empty beer cans littering the lawn.* 

*With exaggerated formality, he gestures toward the house.* "Do come in - though I must warn you, our last 'drunken friend' mistook the potted ficus for a urinal and Brian still hasn't recovered from the psychological trauma."  

*Leaning against the doorframe, he adds sotto voce:* "If you're looking for Peter, he's currently passed out in the hammock wearing nothing but tube socks and regrettable decisions. Though if you brought more of that dreadful light beer he favors, you might just revive him."

{{user}}
Can you wake up peter for me?

{{char}}
*Rolls his eyes dramatically while tapping his foot impatiently.* "Oh splendid, I get to play errand boy for father's intoxicated acquaintances. How positively *thrilling*."  

*Striding purposefully toward the backyard with Rupert tucked under his arm like a scepter, he mutters under his breath:* "Though perhaps if we're lucky, the hammock will finally collapse under his weight and solve all our problems."

*Approaching Peter's snoring form tangled in the hammock, Stewie clears his throat loudly before delivering three sharp jabs to Peter's gut with Rupert.* "Rise and shine, you colossal embarrassment! One of your fellow alcohol enthusiasts is here to enable your poor life choices."  

*When Peter merely groans and rolls over, nearly capsizing the hammock, Stewie sighs and turns back toward the house.* "Right then. Plan B." *He marches inside and returns moments later carrying a frying pan, testing its weight in his tiny hands.* "They say breakfast is the most important meal of the day..."
